# Steam Games Manager
# Automatically import Epic / GOG / Xbox games into Steam as non-Steam shortcuts
# with SteamGridDB artwork.

## Request-body review (errors / inconsistencies fixed)

| # | Issue in original brief | Resolution implemented |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Epic `LaunchOptions` given as `-com.epicgames.launcher://apps/...` (leading dash) and "`Exe` = binary **or** protocol URL". | `Exe` must always be a filesystem executable. Fixed to `Exe=<EpicGamesLauncher.exe>`, `LaunchOptions=com.epicgames.launcher://apps/<AppName>?action=launch&silent=true` (no leading `-`). Code: `scanners/epic.py:build_epic_shortcut`. |
| 2 | GOG flags `/gameId=<ID> /command=runGame`. | Galaxy expects `/command=runGame /gameId=<ID>`. Both orders work, but canonical order implemented: `scanners/gog.py`. |
| 3 | Xbox `Exe = explorer.exe shell:AppsFolder\...` conflated. | Split correctly: `Exe=C:\Windows\explorer.exe`, `LaunchOptions=shell:AppsFolder\<FamilyName>!<AppId>`. Code: `scanners/xbox.py`. |
| 4 | Grid naming `<AppID>p.jpg / <AppID>_hero.jpg / <AppID>_logo.png / <AppID>.ico`. | First three are correct Steam grid names. `<AppID>.ico` is **not** a grid file — icon lives wherever you cache it and `shortcuts.vdf → icon` points at it. Implemented: grid files go to `config/grid/`, icon cached to `config/grid/<appid>.ico` (also accepted by Steam) and referenced absolutely. Code: `artwork/steamgriddb.py`, `vdf_handler/appid.py`. |
| 5 | "Calculate AppID using CRC32/SHA1". | SHA1 is not used. Canonical algorithm is `appid = crc32(exe + appname) | 0x80000000` (unsigned 32-bit). Implemented + unit-verified in `vdf_handler/appid.py`. |
| 6 | `vdf` vs `steam-vdf`, binary safety, Steam-running guard. | Wrapper prefers installed `vdf` package (`binary_loads/dumps`), falls back to bundled pure-Python `binary_vdf.py`. Every write makes a timestamped `.bak`, checks `steam.exe` via `psutil` → `tasklist` → `pgrep`. Code: `vdf_handler/shortcuts.py`, `utils/process.py`. |
| 7 | Cross-platform claim vs Win-only sources (registry, UWP, PROGRAMDATA). | All scanners degrade gracefully on Linux: return `[]` with a warning; Proton path resolution helper included in `config.py`. |
| 8 | `icon` field casing. | Brief is correct: VDF key is lowercase `icon`, rest CamelCase. Preserved exactly. |

## File structure

```
steam_games_manager/
    __init__.py
    __main__.py
    main.py              # CLI entry (argparse)
    config.py            # Steam path / userdata / SteamID resolution
    models.py            # GameInfo dataclass
    scanners/
        __init__.py
        base.py          # Scanner protocol + helpers
        epic.py          # %PROGRAMDATA%\Epic\...\Manifests\*.item
        gog.py           # registry HKLM\...\GOG.com\Games + galaxy-2.0.db
        xbox.py          # Get-AppxPackage via PowerShell
    vdf_handler/
        __init__.py
        appid.py         # CRC32 shortcut AppID
        binary_vdf.py    # dependency-free binary VDF codec (fallback)
        shortcuts.py     # load/merge/write shortcuts.vdf safely
    artwork/
        __init__.py
        steamgriddb.py   # search + download grids/heros/logos/icons
    utils/
        __init__.py
        process.py       # is_steam_running()
        files.py         # backup, atomic write, quoting
tests/
    test_appid.py
    test_binary_vdf.py
    test_epic.py
requirements.txt
README.md  (this file)
```

## Usage

```powershell
pip install -e .
# or
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Dry run — scan only
python -m steam_games_manager --dry-run --verbose

# Full import with artwork (will prompt for SteamGridDB key if omitted)
python -m steam_games_manager --api-key SGDB_KEY --launchers epic,gog,xbox

# Non-interactive, specific user, force overwrite without Steam-running abort
python -m steam_games_manager --user-id 12345678 --no-prompt --force
```

Steam must be **closed** before writing. The tool aborts if `steam.exe`
is running unless `--force` is passed.
